From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsHelperGuards <kmshg@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:40:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0110] gpu31-kms: guard optional atomic-helper callbacks (int68, module-only)

int67 hits another NULL deref, this time inside our M0 helper backport:

    PC is at 0x0
    LR is at drm_atomic_helper_commit_post_planes+0x144/0x144 [drm_kms_helper]

`commit_post_planes` has the shape

    if (funcs->enable)
            funcs->enable(x);
    else
            funcs->commit(x);        /* commit is optional upstream */

and our DSI encoder has neither .enable nor .commit (the link enable lives in
the CRTC), so the else branch jumps to NULL.

Every `funcs->X()` call site in the backport is now either guarded or on an
operation upstream makes mandatory:

  - commit_post_planes: CRTC and encoder `else -> else if (funcs->commit)`
    (commit is optional in upstream 4.0);
  - disable_outputs: CRTC and encoder `else -> else if (funcs->dpms)` (the
    legacy dpms fallback is optional; the chain still prefers prepare/disable);
  - crtc_set_mode: `if (funcs->mode_set)` around the encoder hook (int67's
    no-op still provides it, but the helper no longer relies on that);
  - plane commit: `else if (funcs->atomic_update)` (atomic_disable/update pair);
  - already guarded before this patch: prepare/cleanup_fb, atomic_check,
    atomic_begin/atomic_flush, mode_set_nofb/CRTC mode_set;
  - still unguarded, and mandatory per upstream (documented): connector
    .best_encoder, encoder/CRTC .mode_fixup (encoder only when .atomic_check is
    absent), and the guarded-by-contract atomic_update on planes that do not
    implement atomic_disable.

`drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c` is part of drm_kms_helper, which is a
module in this configuration, so the built-in image is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c
@@ -601,7 +601,7 @@
 			funcs->prepare(encoder);
 		else if (funcs->disable)
 			funcs->disable(encoder);
-		else
+		else if (funcs->dpms)
 			funcs->dpms(encoder, DRM_MODE_DPMS_OFF);
 	}
 
@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@
 			funcs->prepare(crtc);
 		else if (funcs->disable)
 			funcs->disable(crtc);
-		else
+		else if (funcs->dpms)
 			funcs->dpms(crtc, DRM_MODE_DPMS_OFF);
 	}
 }
@@ -752,7 +752,8 @@
 		 * Each encoder has at most one connector (since we always steal
 		 * it away), so we won't call call mode_set hooks twice.
 		 */
-		funcs->mode_set(encoder, mode, adjusted_mode);
+		if (funcs->mode_set)
+			funcs->mode_set(encoder, mode, adjusted_mode);
 	}
 }
 
@@ -810,7 +811,7 @@
 
 			if (funcs->enable)
 				funcs->enable(crtc);
-			else
+			else if (funcs->commit)
 				funcs->commit(crtc);
 		}
 	}
@@ -840,7 +841,7 @@
 		 */
 		if (funcs->enable)
 			funcs->enable(encoder);
-		else
+		else if (funcs->commit)
 			funcs->commit(encoder);
 	}
 }
@@ -1168,7 +1169,7 @@
 		if (drm_atomic_plane_disabling(plane, old_plane_state) &&
 		    funcs->atomic_disable)
 			funcs->atomic_disable(plane, old_plane_state);
-		else
+		else if (funcs->atomic_update)
 			funcs->atomic_update(plane, old_plane_state);
 	}
 
